# P1: the device profile of the TIMED four-card verify (c2-packed-tp4-speed: the verify's T1/T2 audits OFF, the drafter's K/V slide ON).
# ONE job: status, an all-four reset, the tp4-prof image (the replay-count read-back hook, QWEN_FAST_PROFILE_DUMP_EVERY), then two gate
# arms on the SAME four real-text prompts (4,096 / 8,192 / 16,384 / 24,576 tokens, every user at the draft-history steady state; user 0
# has 192 tokens out, users 1-3 have 64, all ignore_eos; the shapes are fixed in scripts/ci/ops_profile_plan.py, not here):
#   ops-twin   unprofiled: the per-round trace_ms, the [PACKED-*] phase split and the texts (the perturbation reference and the text
#              reference)
#   ops-trace  profiled: tracy (v138's recipe), op-support 20000 (200000 segfaults the dispatch thread: any other count is refused),
#              the CPP post-process only (no raw device log, which is tens of GB), a read-back after every 2nd verify replay of ANY
#              kind (packed or sequential) so no window overflows the per-core buffer, no prefill flush. One container gives 4-live
#              64-row rounds, then 3- and 2-live padded rounds as users 1-3 finish, then user 0 alone on the 1/2/4-row sequential
#              engines (a lone user has no 16-row step on this profile: the analysis composes it from the 4-row step and the block).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on
# a throwaway commit of tp4/profile and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. ONE IMAGE FOR THE JOB: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image the build step makes from this same commit.
# NEVER CANCEL this job once the gate step has started: the profiler writes as root, and a cancel can leave root-owned files that break
# the next checkout (the always() hand-back step keeps the report and prunes, but a killed container can still be writing). A
# segfault in read_core_data_from_completion_queue is INFRA: do not raise op-support.
# Duration (estimate): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 (up to 12); build 18 typical (at most 90); ops-twin 15-40 (engine build, four
# prefills, about 50 rounds and steps); ops-trace 30-60 (a cold JIT of every profiler-define kernel, the same streams, about 25
# read-backs, the close): 1.5 / 2.5 / 3.5 hours. The gate refuses to start if its worst case (ops-twin 65 min, ops-trace 105 min, plus
# overhead per arm) does not fit the step and job time left.
# Read: the provenance report; per arm, the launched-argv line (profile c2-packed-tp4-speed, QWEN_FAST_TP=4, QWEN_FAST_VERIFY_T1_AUDIT=0,
# QWEN_FAST_VERIFY_T2_AUDIT=0 and, on ops-trace, the profiler variables); no '[PINDIAG] verify t1/t2 audit' line; the '[PINDIAG]
# device profiler read back after replay' lines (at least 20); ops-trace texts == ops-twin texts (profiling must not change arithmetic);
# gate/ops/tp4-profile-report.{json,md}. Then, on the downloaded artifact:
#   python3 scripts/ci/tp4_profile_report.py --results <the artifact's gate/ directory>
# STOP on an attach refusal, a hang, garbage text, or ops-trace texts differing from ops-twin (a real finding).
# SOFT otherwise: the product is data. A report that finds fewer than 8 complete 4-live verify sessions on all chips says so in the plan's
# lines and the job still passes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prof-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-twin,ops-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
